# 01 — Viewport 3D Module Architecture

## 1. Foundational Premise: Cuboids vs Tetrahedra, Nothing Else Differs

The **only** rendering difference between FDM and FEM is the primitive:

| | FDM | FEM |
|---|---|---|
| **Cell shape** | Cuboid (axis-aligned voxel) | Tetrahedron (unstructured) |
| **Topology source** | Structured grid descriptor (shape + origin + spacing) | Binary topology (FMMT: positions + indices + boundaryFaces) |
| **Normals** | Implicit (cube faces) | Computed from boundary face triangles |
| **Field location** | Cell-center values | Node values or cell values |

Everything else — camera, layers, picking, selection, quantity switching, coloring, clipping, glyph rendering, LOD — is **identical**. This is the v1 lesson learned: the mistake was forking the renderer instead of forking only the geometry-builder.

### Design rule

```
DomainAdapter.buildCellGeometry() → THREE.BufferGeometry
```

The adapter returns a standard `BufferGeometry`. The renderer never asks "is this FDM or FEM?".

## 2. Universe / Multi-Object Model

The simulation space has a hierarchical structure that the viewport must understand from day one:

```
Universe
  ├── Object A (ferromagnet, e.g. disk)
  │     └── mesh part(s) → topology → field values
  ├── Object B (ferromagnet, e.g. waveguide)
  │     └── mesh part(s) → topology → field values
  └── Airbox (optional, non-magnetic volume)
        └── mesh part(s) → topology (no field for non-interacting)
```

### Backend API mapping

| Concept | API endpoint | Resource |
|---|---|---|
| Scene with all objects | `GET /model/scene` | Object list, universe config |
| Object list | `GET /model/objects` | Object IDs, names, materials |
| Single object | `GET /model/objects/{object_id}` | Geometry, material, interactions |
| Object topology | `GET /meshing/meshes/objects/{object_id}/topology` | Binary FMMT per object |
| Shared domain topology | `GET /meshing/meshes/shared-domain/topology` | Binary FMMT full domain |
| Universe | `GET /model/universe` | Bounds, airbox config |
| Domain meta | `GET /data/domain/meta` | Discretization, grid, bounds, generation_id |
| Full domain topology | `GET /data/domain/topology` | Binary FMMT solver domain |
| Field data | `GET /data/fields/{qty}/samples/vector` | Binary field vector |
| Visualization state | `GET /visualization/state` | Layers, quantity, sampling, clip, scopes |
| Visualization scope | `VisualizationScopeKind` | `full` / `magnetic` / `airbox` / `object` / `part` / `selection` |
| Vector domain scope | `VectorLayerDomain` | `auto` / `magnetic_only` / `full_domain` / `airbox_only` / `object` / `part` |

### Viewport implications

1. The viewport must render **multiple objects** as distinct selectable entities within one scene.
2. Each object can have a different material color / per-object highlight.
3. Airbox is a separate layer with its own visibility toggle — some simulations have no airbox.
4. Clicking on a face/cell must identify which **object** it belongs to (via element markers or boundary markers in the FMMT topology).
5. Field data may be scoped: full domain, magnetic only, single object, single part, or selection.

